samba-powershell (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read the directory directly over LDAP with the caller's Kerberos ticket.
    The package no longer depends on samba-adws, and a domain controller no
    longer needs the ADWS service.
  * Depend on python3-ldap and libsasl2-modules-gssapi-mit.
  * -Server host names the LDAP port, 389, unless it says otherwise.

 -- CaracalC <martin.ptit@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0400

samba-powershell (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: the SambaAD PowerShell module, with Get-ADUser,
    Get-ADComputer, Get-ADGroup and Get-ADObject, and its Python backend.
  * Install the module under /usr/share/samba-powershell/Modules and link it
    into the PowerShell all-users module path from postinst.

 -- CaracalC <martin.ptit@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:30:00 -0400
